From 37815b0084143732013d393e2ba7f21710d867db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:45:28 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] [ADTSSampleReader] Seek to the target sample after a
 reset

A seek into another segment resets the reader, which sets the ADTS PTS
to ADTS_PTS_UNSET. That value is above every target, so
ADTSReader::SeekTime() read no packet and the stream continued at the
segment start. With separate HLS audio and video segments, audio then
started up to one segment before the video: "Seek time 1128.4 ...
continues at 1121.3". Amlogic decoders output no picture until the
clock reaches the video, which froze playback for several seconds.

Backport the ADTS part of upstream e727bae22d ("[samplereader] Fix read
sample on seek") and e15a188da0 ("[SampleReaders] Fix bad EOS return
state"): read the first sample before the scan, so the segment's first
packet sets the PTS diff, publish the sample the scan stops at, and
return false at the end of the stream. Omega passes the seek time in
the stream's own timestamps, so the upstream "pts += m_ptsDiff" is not
needed here.

Initialize the ID3 timestamp, which the reader read uninitialized for
audio without ID3 tags.
